Kit 1.0.0 is usable (2026-11-15). Read video/README.md (workflow + rules) and video/kit/README.md (catalog). Entry points, all run from /home/claude/demos-all/video: `node kit/scripts/new-film.mjs <slug> --company "Name"` scaffolds films/<slug>/ on the retention-first template (cold open -> footage scene(s) -> next steps -> end card + one captions host) and vendors the kit into films/<slug>/kit/ (re-vendor after kit edits with `node kit/scripts/sync.mjs <slug>`; never edit the film's kit/ copy); `node kit/scripts/build-footage.mjs films/<slug> --import <clip>=/path/old.mp4 [--marks <clip>=marks.json] [--boxes <clip>=boxes.json]` brings existing footage in (new takes: write capture/record.cjs on kit/scripts/capture.cjs, which records DOM boxes, then `build-footage.mjs films/<slug>`), and capture/cuts.json makes the 2 s `hook` clip the cold-open block plays; legacy footage without DOM boxes gets boxes from `python3 kit/scripts/measure-boxes.py <clip.mp4> spec.json --debug dir` (snaps rough boxes to card edges; check the overlays) or a hand-written {samples:[{name,t,x,y,w,h}]} file; `node kit/scripts/qa.mjs films/<slug> [--frames | --video renders/x.mp4]` is the gate (duration < 60 s, first product frame <= 2 s, text cards <= 2 s, end card <= 3 s, every camera keyframe and ring framed whole inside the safe area = frame minus 24 px minus the caption band y>=840, every speed change labelled) and writes renders/qa/contact-sheet.jpg + framing-sheet.jpg. A film consumes the kit like this: index.html <head> loads gsap, kit/tokens.css, kit/kit.css, kit/kit.js and data/clips.js; blocks mount directly as hosts with fixed ids (coldopen, title, nextsteps, endcard) via data-composition-src="kit/blocks/<name>.html" plus data-variable-values JSON for the text (*word* = the cyan word) and data-kit-role; footage scenes are the film's own compositions/*.html built from kit/components/footage-scene.html: <video class="clip kit-footage" data-kit-clip="<clip>" ...> inside .kit-stage > .kit-cam, camera keyframes as JSON in <script type="application/json" class="kit-shots">[{"t":0,"focus":"<component>"}, ...]</script> (focus = a tracked component name; "partial": true needs a "reason"), rings as <div class="clip kit-ring" data-kit-focus="<component>">, and one call `Kit.scene.footage({ id: "<scene>", tl })` before registering the timeline; captions are compositions/captions.html from kit/components/caption-band.html (cues = .kit-cap clips, speed tags = <span class="kit-speed" data-rate="6" data-tag-start data-tag-end>6x</span>, honesty labels = .kit-chip) animated by `Kit.captions.animate(tl, "captions")`. Do not tween .kit-cam by hand (QA fails it). Kit changes after this point are additive and logged in video/kit/CHANGELOG.md. Reference film (being built now): video/films/distru/.
